  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: named could terminate unexpectedly when concurrent messages signed or verified with the same GSS-TSIG key raced on its shared security context\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-94300.patch: serialize access to the shared GSS-TSIG security context (upstream 1d93eddce0)\n     - CVE-2026-94300\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: a crafted DNS message could make named spend disproportionate CPU time following chains of name compression pointers\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19630.patch: limit how many compression pointers a name and a message may make named follow (upstream e6a38e901d); keeps the budget out of struct dns_decompress to preserve the libdns1104 ABI\n     - CVE-2026-19630",
